-- title:
--   Root–fibre criterion for partial G/partial Y≠ 0, separable case
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and suppose there is $x_0\in F$ such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x_0)$ generated by $x_0$. Assume every place of $F$ over $K$ is rational, a place being a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\operatorname{im}(K\to F)$, different from $F$ and a principal ideal ring, and rationality meaning that $K$ surjects onto its residue field; for a place $v$ and $f$ in its valuation subring, $v.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in K$ denotes the residue of $f$ pulled back along this surjection (and $0$ otherwise), while $v.\mathrm{ord}$ is the normalised order function attached to $v$. Let $z,y\in F$ with $z$ transcendental over $K$ and $F$ separable over $K(z)$, and let $G\in K[Z][Y]$ be irreducible whose image in $F[Z][Y]$ vanishes at $Z=z$, $Y=y$. Let $Q$ be a place with $z,y$ in its valuation subring such that $\operatorname{ord}_Q(z-Q.\mathrm{evalAt}\,z)=1$, the leading coefficient of $G$ in $Y$ does not vanish at $Q.\mathrm{evalAt}\,z$, and $y$ separates $Q$ in its fibre: every place $Q'\neq Q$ containing $z$ and $y$ with $Q'.\mathrm{evalAt}\,z=Q.\mathrm{evalAt}\,z$ satisfies $Q'.\mathrm{evalAt}\,y\neq Q.\mathrm{evalAt}\,y$. Then the $Y$-derivative of $G$, evaluated at $Z=Q.\mathrm{evalAt}\,z$, $Y=Q.\mathrm{evalAt}\,y$, is nonzero.
--
--   This is the root–fibre lemma for function fields in one variable, asserting that a place which is unramified over $z$ and isolated in its fibre by the value of $y$ gives a simple point of the plane model $G=0$; it is the separable counterpart of the version stated for $K$ of characteristic zero. It is used in the construction of regular prolongations and, in the modular setting, for the models attached to the $j$-line and to $j\circ(N\cdot)$.
